                "retweet_count": 5,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Last year alone, the GAO identified $31 billion in Medicaid improper payments. That is nearly equal to the state budgets of Arkansas, Delaware, Idaho, Vermont, New Hampshire, and South Dakota combined.\n\nIn Medicaid, improper payments are often the result of a costly combination of lax oversight and blatant fraud: unverified documents, false income claims, and missing household information that never gets flagged or fixed.",
